# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Assignment 1A - .gitignore
#
# Rule of thumb: commit what is graded or hand-written; ignore what is large,
# downloaded, or regenerable by re-running the notebook.
#
# Note: .gitignore has NO inline comments - '#' only starts a comment at the
# start of a line - so every note below sits on its own line. A trailing
# comment would silently become part of the pattern and match nothing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- PDFs ------------------------------------------------------------------
# PDFs are ignored by default, with ONE exception: raw_pdfs/ is committed on
# purpose. Those 8 files are the exact input Step 1 was run against, so keeping
# them in the repo means the notebook stays reproducible even if a source URL
# rots - and assignments 1B/2A/2B/2C reuse this same corpus. ~28 MB total,
# largest single file ~10 MB, comfortably inside GitHub's limits.
#
# The '!' rule must come AFTER '*.pdf' - the last matching rule wins. Note also
# that raw_pdfs/ is NOT listed as an ignored directory: git never descends into
# an ignored directory, so a negation inside one would have no effect.

!raw_pdfs/*.pdf

# The assignment briefs stay out - they're re-downloadable from Canvas.
briefs/

# --- Model artifacts: hundreds of MB to several GB, never belong in git -----
cpt_ckpt/
adapter/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt

# --- Regenerable intermediates ---------------------------------------------
# Step 2 packed dataset - rebuild it from domain_corpus/
*.parquet
# Stats and plots - the notebook already prints all of this inline
outputs/

# --- Python / Jupyter ------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored - the graded deliverables plus the source corpus:
#   Assignment1A.ipynb         notebook WITH outputs
#   Assignment1A.html          exported HTML
#   domain_corpus/*.txt        cleaned corpus (1.4 MB, safe for git)
#   instruction_dataset.jsonl  B1 output
#   raw_pdfs/*.pdf             source PDFs, kept for reproducibility
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
